This project involves ethical hacking activities focused on understanding and analyzing system and network security. It includes different phases such as reconnaissance, enumeration, and controlled security testing to identify possible vulnerabilities in a target system. The tools used, such as Nmap, Zenmap, and Bettercap, help in scanning networks, gathering information, and simulating security assessments in a legal and controlled environment. The main objective of this activity is to improve cybersecurity awareness and strengthen system defenses against potential cyber threats.
